    "field": "Solar-climate interactions",
    "problem": "Climate models poorly represent the relationship between the 11-year solar cycle and the North Atlantic Oscillation (NAO), a detection complicated by the NAO's own intrinsic quasi-decadal fluctuations that can mask the externally forced solar signal.",
    "method": "By comparing two multi-decadal climate model simulations, one with and one without solar forcing variability, the authors demonstrate that the 11-year solar cycle synchronizes the intrinsic quasi-decadal variability of the North Atlantic Oscillation through downward propagation from the stratosphere.",
    "task": "The task is to determine if the 11-year solar cycle synchronizes intrinsic quasi-decadal variability of the North Atlantic Oscillation by comparing climate model simulations performed with and without variable solar forcing.",
